Package: manimR
Title: Mathematical Animation Engine, a Native R Port of 'Manim'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Adam R", "Sophie", , "adamrsophie@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Create precise programmatic animations for explanatory math videos,
    in the style of 'Manim Community' <https://www.manim.community/>, written in
    pure R. Scenes are built from vectorized mobjects made of cubic Bezier curves,
    animated with transforms, creations, fades, and updaters, and rendered to
    video, GIF, or PNG through 'ffmpeg'. Includes text rendered from system fonts,
    LaTeX via 'dvisvgm', SVG import, graphing tools, a 3D camera, and 'RStudio'
    addins. The design and algorithms follow the Python 'manim' library by the
    Manim Community developers, whose work is gratefully acknowledged.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Copyright: See the file inst/COPYRIGHTS for the copyright holders of
    Manim Community, NetworkX, earcut.hpp and isosurfaces, whose code this
    package ports.
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE, r6 = FALSE)
Depends:
    R (>= 4.4.0)
Imports:
    R6,
    grid,
    grDevices,
    ragg,
    systemfonts (>= 1.2.0),
    textshaping,
    xml2,
    png,
    digest,
